              "html": "Conservationists in the Sahel, the semi-arid region along the southern edge of the Sahara, have planted large numbers of drought-resistant trees as part of the Great Green Wall initiative. The trees’ roots hold loose soil in place and help the ground absorb rainwater. Project leaders hope that, over time, the planting will arrest the spread of the desert into nearby farmland."
